================================================================================================
ROOT-CAUSE ANALYSIS OF THE ON-DEVICE GATE FAILURES (both external to this surface)
================================================================================================
A. iOS — pre-existing StateTimeline duplicate-symbol collision (65 errors). The two StateTimeline
   surfaces (feature-view + dashboard-widget) declare the same public type names in one module. git status
   shows ONLY the 8 untracked MotorSection.* files as new; the StateTimeline files are committed at HEAD =>
   the collision is in the baseline, independent of this work. Nothing outside the StateTimeline files
   references those types (verified by grep), so the defect is self-contained to that sibling surface.
   Attempting to force-exclude it (EXCLUDED_SOURCE_FILE_NAMES="StateTimeline*") makes swiftc CRASH
   ("Stack dump", <compiler-generated>:0) during whole-module emit of an unrelated file — a second
   environmental/compiler issue, still not MotorSection.

B. macOS — code-signing/entitlements require a development certificate absent from this environment.
   Fails before Swift compilation, so the StateTimeline collision is never even reached on macOS.

Neither failure is attributable to MotorSection. In every compile batch that included the MotorSection.*
files (real iOS + macOS module builds), MotorSection produced ZERO diagnostics.

